-Activation facts (from `benchmark/results/validation-report-2026-08-30.md`):
+## What it does
 
-- With this plugin attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot immediately fails with `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)` and exit 1;
-- After migrating per the skill card (`inject: ["llm"]` + `ctx.llm.listProviders()` + removing the dead dependency), activation succeeds; with no API key in the container, a route count of 0 is expected — as long as the calls go through.
+- Ships as a bundle: `package.json#dsh.bundle.patch` points at `cordis.patch.yml`, so a profile that
+  lists `@demo/dsh-upgrade-demo` in `dsh.profile.bundles` composes that patch and inserts the plugin
+  row (entry id `upgrade-demo`).
+- On activation, injects the host `llm` service and logs `ctx.llm.listProviders()` — the registered
+  provider routes in registration order — or a failure line when the call throws.
+
+## Activation facts
+
+- With this plugin attached, dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 cold boot succeeds: the `upgrade-demo` row activates on
+  the `llm` service and the boot proceeds to the model call.
+- With no API key in the container, a route count of 0 is expected — as long as the calls go through.
+- Historical (0.1.1-rc.2-era code, `inject: ["apiProxy"]` + `ctx.apiProxy.llm.providers()`): the same
+  cold boot failed immediately with `plugin tree failed ... pending (waiting for service: apiProxy)`
+  and exit 1. The package that provided `ctx.apiProxy` (`@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy`) is not
+  published after 0.1.1-rc.2.
+
+## Migration mapping
+
+| 0.1.1-rc.2 era | 0.1.2-alpha.2 |
+| --- | --- |
+| `export const inject = ["apiProxy"]` | `export const inject = ["llm"]` |
+| `await ctx.apiProxy.llm.providers()` | `ctx.llm.listProviders()` |
+| dependency `@deepseek-ai/dsh-host-apiproxy@0.0.1-rc.1` | removed (no host package provides it) |
